% NEGATIVE: a `when` mask on a CROSS gather is not an array_dv operation.
%
% Masking COMPACTS -- `for i in 1,6 returns array_dv of i when mod(i,2)=0` gives
% [2,4,6], three of six.  A cross gather's result is rectangular (i_ext x j_ext),
% so masking it makes the shape ragged: how many survive is a property of the
% DATA, not of the extents.  array_dv is strictly sized, so there is no array_dv
% answer here.
%
% This used to compile and SILENTLY DROP the mask (returning all four elements,
% [11,12,21,22], instead of [12,21]).  The IF1 does carry the mask -- a cross
% builds a nested RETURNS and the mask rides the INNER gather -- but the lowering
% only consulted the outer one.
%
% The alternatives are in the error message: give the result an explicit extent
% when the size is known, or accumulate into a list and pack it once (what
% e2e/backtrack_dv.sis does for a walk whose length is unknown until it ends).
define main
type A = array_dv[integer];

function main( returns A )
  for i in 1, 2 cross j in 1, 2
  returns array_dv of i*10 + j when (i + j) = 3
  end for
end function
